"""
D2 sensitivity check (report only): the stance search of experiments/stance_two_points.py rerun with ONE thing changed at a time. Nothing in the layout, the staging pose or the settings
is changed; the cases only change the search's own copy of the object positions and grasp settings.

    source .venv/bin/activate
    MUJOCO_GL=egl python experiments/stance_sensitivity.py --case baseline [--out data/d2/sens] [--smoke]
    (cases: baseline edge12 edge8 level10 margin5 mid4 warm; experiments/stance_sensitivity.sh runs them one after the other)

Cases (beaker and hotplate stay 20 cm apart; "edge" distances are the objects' centre to the bench's front edge, currently 14 cm):
  baseline  the current settings, on the grid below (the grid is wider in x than the first D2 run, whose best stances sat at its x edge)
  edge12    beaker and hotplate centres 12 cm from the bench edge (hotplate front 3 cm from the edge)
  edge8     8 cm from the edge (the 18 cm deep hotplate then overhangs the edge by 1 cm)
  level10   level tolerance 10 degrees instead of 5
  margin5   joint margin 5 degrees instead of 10
  mid4      only the 4 middle grasp heights (35, 40, 45, 50 % of the beaker's height) instead of 8: 12 points instead of 24
  open      the bench is open below its top (what-if; the scene is not changed): its four frame rails are left out and only the top and the legs remain, so the base may drive partly under
            the bench. The stance y is then searched from 8 cm outside the edge to 32 cm under it (footprint clearance +8 to -32 cm), a stance must have the whole robot (both arms at home,
            the neck at its drive pose) clear of the bench top and legs, and so must the shifted stances of the tolerance checks. The result file also has the deepest the base gets under
            the bench at x 0.75 and headings -90 and -100 for each pedestal height (first contact when driving in 1 cm at a time) and where the torso's front is then.
  warm      the IK check of stage 2 and of the margins also starts from the solutions of neighbouring points (the next height, the set-down below the 'above' point, the grasp
            of the same height) after the random starts, so it can only find more than the random starts; stage 1 keeps stances that reach 5 of the 6 extreme points (not all 6), so
            the stance-level false negatives of stage 1 show too. The result file also holds the counts the random starts alone give on the same candidates.

Stages: 1 coarse grid with the 6 extreme points; 2 all points, collision-free against the robot itself (as before) and, in addition, the hand and fingers (and, separately, the whole arm)
clear of the bench and the hotplate; 3 margins of the best survivors of each heading (2 at -90 and -100, 1 at the others): joint margin, xy tolerance up to 8 cm, heading up to +-8 degrees,
pedestal +-4.2 cm (as before but the xy and heading caps are higher because the old caps of 5 cm and 4 degrees were reached), and the furniture check of those stances.
The furniture check holds the open gripper (the staging opening) at each solution; the held beaker is not part of it.
"""

